      "role": "user",
      "content": "Implement the following requested change in the repository.\n\n# Missing PyFlakes message in FLAKE8_PYFLAKES_CODES mapping\n\n### Bug summary\nThe `FLAKE8_PYFLAKES_CODES` dictionary in `src/flake8/plugins/pyflakes.py` is missing a mapping for the PyFlakes message \"ContinueInFinally\".\n\n### Code for reproduction\n\n```python\nimport flake8.plugins.pyflakes as pyflakes_shim\nimport pyflakes.messages\n\n# Get all PyFlakes message classes\nmessages = {name for (name, obj) in vars(pyflakes.messages).items() \n            if name[0].isupper() and obj.message}\n\n# Check if all messages have codes assigned\nmissing = messages - set(pyflakes_shim.FLAKE8_PYFLAKES_CODES)\nprint(f\"Missing messages: {missing}\")\n```\n\n### Actual outcome\n\nThe script prints:\n```\nMissing messages: {'ContinueInFinally'}\n```\n\nThis indicates that the PyFlakes message \"ContinueInFinally\" exists in the PyFlakes library but doesn't have a corresponding Flake8 error code assigned in the `FLAKE8_PYFLAKES_CODES` dictionary.\n\n### Expected outcome\n\nAll PyFlakes messages should have corresponding Flake8 error codes. The script should print:\n```\nMissing messages: set()\n```\n\nThis issue could cause Flake8 to miss reporting \"continue\" statements inside \"finally\" blocks, which is a potential bug in Python code.\n\nScope of this editing session: update the following production files and submit the resulting local patch: src/flake8/plugins/pyflakes.py. No full task validation has been performed in this session."
    },
